Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: vyos-http-api-tools
Upstream-Contact: VyOS Package Maintainers <maintainers@vyos.net>
Source: https://github.com/vyos/vyos-http-api-tools
Comment:
 The binary package is a Python virtual environment built with dh-virtualenv
 that bundles the third-party Python packages pinned in requirements.txt.
 Their versions change with that file. Each bundled package installs its own
 license and copyright notice in its *.dist-info/ directory under
 /usr/share/vyos-http-api-tools/lib/python3*/site-packages/.
 .
 All of them are under permissive licenses:
 .
  - MIT: annotated-doc, annotated-types, anyio, fastapi, graphql-core, h11,
    httptools, pydantic, pydantic-core, pyjwt, python-pam, pyyaml,
    typing-inspection, watchfiles, wsproto
  - BSD-3-Clause: ariadne, click, idna, makefun, python-dotenv, starlette,
    uvicorn, websockets
  - Apache-2.0: opentelemetry-api, python-multipart
  - MIT or Apache-2.0: uvloop
  - ISC: sgqlc
  - PSF-2.0: typing-extensions

